# Project Read-Map

Global doctrine is already loaded from `~/.cursor/rules/profile/`. The documents below
are **not** loaded — `AI_PROFILE/**` and `.cursor/repo-context/**` are never auto-read.
Open them with the Read tool before writing code that touches the listed area.

| Task touches | MUST read first |
|---|---|
| `centos/`, `debian-nft/`, or `debian-ufw/` refresh scripts, or a `dynhosts.json.example` / `zones.json.example` | `.cursor/repo-context/architecture-decisions.md`, `.cursor/repo-context/dangerous-areas.md`, `.cursor/repo-context/known-constraints.md`, `.cursor/repo-context/patterns-and-antipatterns.md` |
| README install or operator behavior | `.cursor/repo-context/known-constraints.md`, `.cursor/repo-context/architecture-decisions.md` |

`AI_PROFILE/languages/` has no shell guide. Do not borrow the php or powershell guides for these scripts.

Project docs in `.cursor/repo-context/` outrank portable doctrine on conflict.
